{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_intro_why_actors_shared_mutable_state_problem", "label": "Geteilter veraenderlicher State unter Nebenlaeufigkeit", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "Das Promise-/async-await-Modell gibt Parallelitaet, aber kein Synchronisationsprimitiv \u2014 zwei nebenlaeufige Einzahlungen lesen beide 0 und eine geht verloren.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/intro/why-actors.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_intro_why_actors_stateful_long_lived_components", "label": "Statusbehaftete langlebige Komponenten", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "Die uebliche Antwort \u2014 Klasse zustandslos machen, State nach Redis/Postgres \u2014 tauscht ein Concurrency-Problem gegen zwei operative: Network-Roundtrips bei jedem Read und denselben Race im Datenspeicher.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/intro/why-actors.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_intro_why_actors_error_recovery_problem", "label": "Fehlererholung ohne Supervision", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "Vanilla JS beantwortet nicht, was mit dem partiellen State nach einem Throw passiert, ob das Objekt noch sicher ist und ob Aufrufer vom Absturz wissen sollten \u2014 man baut es pro Service, meistens inkonsistent.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/intro/why-actors.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_intro_why_actors_actors_encapsulate_state", "label": "Actors kapseln State", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "Innerhalb von onReceive ist garantiert, dass niemand sonst liest oder schreibt \u2014 der Actor ist die Serialisierungsgrenze, count++ braucht keinen Mutex.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/intro/why-actors.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_intro_why_actors_messages_are_the_only_contract", "label": "Nachrichten sind der einzige Vertrag", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "Die scheinbar unnoetige Restriktion macht drei Dinge umsonst: Asynchronitaet (jedes tell ist fire-and-forget), Backpressure (die Mailbox hat eine Laenge und eine waehlbare Policy) und Location Transparency.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/intro/why-actors.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_intro_why_actors_supervisors_first_class", "label": "Supervisors behandeln Fehler als erstklassiges Anliegen", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "Vier Ergebnisse \u2014 Restart, Resume, Stop, Escalate \u2014 einmal pro Actor-Klasse konfiguriert, sodass jeder Fehler gleich behandelt wird.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/intro/why-actors.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_intro_why_actors_when_not_to_use_actors", "label": "Wann Actors NICHT zu verwenden sind", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "Zustandslose Request/Response-Services, reine Datentransformationen und Code, der synchron blockieren muss \u2014 Actor-Overhead ist verschwendet, wo es nichts zu kapseln gibt.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/intro/why-actors.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_intro_why_actors_when_actors_fit", "label": "Wann Actors die richtige Wahl sind", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "State pro Entitaet, der laenger als ein Request lebt; Fehlerisolierung; Verteilung; alles, was konzeptionell ein Zustandsautomat ist. Pointiert: die Kaestchen auf dem Whiteboard sind meistens Actors.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/intro/why-actors.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_intro_why_actors_actors_encapsulate_state", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_intro_why_actors_shared_mutable_state_problem", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/intro/why-actors.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_intro_why_actors_actors_encapsulate_state", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_intro_why_actors_stateful_long_lived_components", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/intro/why-actors.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_intro_why_actors_supervisors_first_class", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_intro_why_actors_error_recovery_problem", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/intro/why-actors.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_intro_why_actors_messages_are_the_only_contract", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_intro_glossary_tell", "relation": "references", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.95, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/intro/why-actors.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 0.95}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_intro_why_actors_messages_are_the_only_contract", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_intro_what_is_actor_ts_location_transparency", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/intro/why-actors.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_intro_why_actors_when_not_to_us